        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0111" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1960: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Chungking</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-12-07T19:00:00-05:00">December 7, 1939—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>231. Your 626, December 4, 5 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department desires that the American Consul General at Shanghai transmit
                        informally and without comment the text of the Chinese <pb facs="0112"
                            n="106" xml:id="pg106"/> Foreign Office’s note to the appropriate
                        authorities of the Shanghai International Settlement.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Please make suitable acknowledgment to the Chinese Foreign Office of its
                        note and say that the note is being communicated to the appropriate
                        authorities of the Shanghai International Settlement.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
